## Summary
Attempt 3 changed only the server-side persons-error classifier
(handlers_rates.go) and its tests, fixing checker-second's attempt-2 catch
(a bare `strings.Contains(msg,"birth_month")` falsely collapsed "birth
month after start date" into "needs a birth month"). All markup/JS/CSS
(rate-assumptions.html, whatif-rate-assumptions.js) is byte-identical to
the already-PASSed attempt 2. Live-traced in both themes: the new "birth
month after start date" message is announced once via role=alert, sits as
the settings form's first child, is truthful (names the person, correctly
says "after" not "needs"), renders with real apostrophes (no raw &#39;
exposed to AT or sighted users -- confirmed via DOM read + screenshot),
passes contrast (5.72:1 light / 8.88:1 dark), and leaves focus on the
edited field with the alert still announcing via role="alert". The
distinct "missing birth month" message remains correctly reachable and
unconflated. Glide checkbox keyboard behavior and the linked-removal
refusal were re-verified unchanged in both themes. axe-core (card
expanded, all 4 states, both themes) found 0 new violations; the one dark-
mode violation is the same pre-existing, out-of-scope node attempt 2
recorded. No FAILURES.
